BT /F1 10 Tf 0 0 0 rg 56 295.69 Td (withdraw\(\) lets the campaign creator take the entire fund balance at any time. The root cause is a missing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0 0 0 rg 56 282.29 Td (business-logic precondition: the function never verifies that the funding goal was met or the deadline passed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0 0 0 rg 56 268.89 Td (before releasing funds. That unguarded path is then executed via direct lamport manipulation Ч the fund) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0 0 0 rg 56 255.49 Td (account is debited and the creator credited by writing lamports directly \(try_borrow_mut_lamports\) instead of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0 0 0 rg 56 242.09 Td (a checked System Program transfer Ч so the withdrawal is both unauthorized by the funding model and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0 0 0 rg 56 228.69 Td (non-atomic. Because there is no goal/deadline gate, a creator can drain contributions before a campaign) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0 0 0 rg 56 215.29 Td (succeeds; because the transfer bypasses the normal CPI path, a partial failure can also leave balances and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0 0 0 rg 56 201.89 Td (accounting inconsistent. The missing precondition and the direct-lamport mechanism share one root cause) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0 0 0 rg 56 188.49 Td (and one fix, so they are reported here as a single finding.) Tj ET
